/T (Text Field49)
/Type /Annot
/V (The analyst involved in the changeover surface sampling plate setup\054 Clea S\056 Garza \050CGS\051\054 and the analysts involved in reading the plate\054 Maraya Chukwumerije and Sophia Santamaria\054 were interviewed comprehensively\056 Their responses are documented throughout this investigation\056\012\012The EM plates were stored in accordance with the supplier\047s recommendations\054 visually inspected before use\054 and verified to be within their assigned expiration dates\056 All materials and supplies were disinfected in accordance with MICRO\055SOP\0559\054 Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology\056 The functionality of the incubators was verified through review of data generated by the in\055house continuous monitoring system\056\012\012Changeover Surface Sampling was performed by Clea S\056 Garza in ISO 5 BSC E001309 located in room 117A in suite CR117 on the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\054 in accordance with MICRO\055SOP\0552\054 Environmental Monitoring of the Cleanroom Facility\056\012\012The plates were initially incubated at a temperature of 30\05535\260C in incubator E001031 for a minimum duration of 48 hours\054 commencing on 11 May 2026\056 Following completion of the minimum 48 hours of incubation on 13 May 2026\054 no microbial growth was observed\056 The plates were subsequently incubated for a minimum of 5 days at 20\05525\260C in incubator E001034\054 with incubation ending on 18 May 2026\056 At completion of the second incubation period\054 one colony\055like artifact was observed on S1\056 The plate was read by Maraya Chukwumerije after the initial incubation period and by Sophia Santamaria after the second incubation period\056 Please see Table 1 for detailed information on the observations during the respective incubations\056\012\012The observed artifact was submitted for microbial identification under ETX\055260518\0550273\056 However\054 following transfer or inoculation onto fresh media\054 no growth was observed\056 Therefore\054 the observed artifact could not be confirmed as a viable microbial colony or reported as a confirmed colony forming unit \050CFU\051\056 The lack of growth upon subculture indicates that the observation may have been nonviable material\054 an artifact associated with agar preparation or pouring\054 or another non\055microbial artifact\056\012\012To evaluate environmental controls and determine whether the recovery was transient or recurring\054 personnel\055monitoring plates for Clea S\056 Garza and ISO 5 BSC E001309 environmental\055monitoring plates were bracketed across the testing period\054 as detailed in Table 2\056)
>>
endobj
